          "type": "response_end",
          "response": {
            "text": "Alberto uses Claude in several of his agent projects:\n\n- **Portfolio Agent** (this site): built on Claude and TypeScript. It answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects, and it is also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it. Its source and eval report are public on GitHub.\n- **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline evals, for an online ticketing platform): it reviews new events and organizers and recommends approve, reject, or request-info for a human admin. In offline evals (31 cases), Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment over a local 9B model, with 86% accuracy versus 71% and 1% of fraud approved versus 8%. It costs about $0.002 per review.\n\nHe also works with Grok and open-source models (cloud and local via Ollama), and his agent practices include offline evals, human-in-the-loop review, and tracked cost and limits.",
